      "text": "Next lesson",
      "hash": "d0ae2a13d8665949dd104a2fbdedcc8bca3e647a1e131d1ebaeb31c189a553b4"
    },
    {
      "id": "ea09e3df6c3b3a0df25566414c93297bdb9d6f417b4f33737e2199366e6f850d",
      "text": "On this page",
      "hash": "b5658fc8edda24f9c94eabac9e536e0a18e3055a8ca255f9d1b8f256ea02a6cc"
    },
    {
      "id": "b0aedffb20d1d4d318b1c937f78e2ac67cf8fcf0b44a7d31c9a9bede95e88c43",
      "text": "One Client At A Time",
      "hash": "f3ee124290893699aa5e3e22209c0101bd0d35003743c71bea2f9ccfa581a165"
    },
    {
      "id": "ad6d946f3e4be819bb014f80e010535107c81d8f67dcc67cbd0212c246746537",
      "text": "Stateful Server",
      "hash": "43b33772f084585d289808fb664866c9e468b03e57e1ca8d48efd89b18b331c7"
    },
    {
      "id": "320049b7b2284b27b6133c57216fb96c4979fb67936e6b37722b539518b71b40",
      "text": "Store The State In Redis",
      "hash": "ac97aec1a34275206ba18a81b0ffe2e93362f5d6b499fca97adfcd41a57e87ce"
    },
    {
      "id": "5988d82594c284a748e5bc1a9695a7a536461123d8a84528a009df7ea9b05abe",
      "text": "Vercel Example",
      "hash": "80b12d0f957ab03685787f5a2d6d65ec1568b8e42dbe02358279257f7e567fc0"
    },
    {
      "id": "0c6316ba6f427d2d8c44ecdecf72eeb928ec5214b7f14a2aa83473f544c275dc",
      "text": "Conclusion",
      "hash": "89db2ad881f29c18b305a20c8ed7bdffdfde49d633c27a83bd204bf9cfedaba3"
    },
    {
      "id": "6e707c7669745b59bb12d340196f163a7ec5770cc7feaa1e93ee39a120d0b4ac",
      "text": "Up next",
      "hash": "e31da5b25f8b7324861e9aadaf5c503e7fd43e739fa3be17ebe63e999fb13df1"
    },
    {
      "id": "e43d9d837cd90e6c8c2f0ca6e19cbabb122bc772031bbcfeb094526c00dfbea9",
      "text": "In a",
      "hash": "cd7e14a97155920e6c47f28027437132fc7827e5f4aaf91f93e54142a004847d"
    },
    {
      "id": "9e685147915e9f7b28bd78199ea00e7332bc322feef0ba1f6dae01ae67be5544",
      "text": "previous example",
      "hash": "20fd82f3a5ea79d10e936dc73cd5bc7e46ee7f862e1978036f572f8f936aab64"
    },
    {
      "id": "80ea4c3849b8e9aaf4883fc82df23b02855618315e0ecae2696d511eb2cd66ee",
      "text": ", we created a simple MCP server that could be served over HTTP.",
      "hash": "bb7c7aeb44712ffe94c8f67b090b469b8d5b822e5ddfe2ec5a8f2b661629712a"
    },
    {
      "id": "1a8320dd2efd74d8ac0b185ea552b6d959508c303b9a930f2b7bf65b28642018",
      "text": "But it had some downsides",
      "hash": "e227e7641d34342fd5bdfc0c85067942c053c8158f3367e1d684dcb03720ab45"
    },
    {
      "id": "a1a30f01945387cc88dd1b8430de898b69ea0839a86b7c4567f962e0acc0533f",
      "text": "The most obvious is that",
      "hash": "a41f77314a58c5bd3e7cbb7645eac142b5998fe42e390a3a277cbf7a381ba21b"
    },
    {
      "id": "9cbd37d3e47797a11b7741823a62b526a2a59de28bbcd5d9eb010e6cb8f7f905",
      "text": "it could only serve one client at a time",
      "hash": "ba57f69d9a59e7e2dd43f5599c6b277b13e613420ada7a55095ea3ab5bbdf535"
    },
    {
      "id": "2185fe12a9cb37739835ecccfeb36991dddf34596431e0034f5d410654efed65",
      "text": ". It saved its current 'transport' in a single variable:",
      "hash": "b05d1f06c96fe68882e2c6dfd948d1a02c92ff786520ce56febae356b878226c"
    },
    {
      "id": "087ad22bed18043a017625bfa6ebe193c5edee4cc007eee93c29f0d66813452a",
      "text": "This meant that if",
      "hash": "a9ce4b3b76ffd2840678e6fe166bd77a9001a1cdd79a087ea1333c5b2f8bf849"
    },
    {
      "id": "1d3168b0d910da9772e97f4ed602618942a0f7edab2e75159af5d34e48bd8d3f",
      "text": "a second client connected, the first client would lose connection",
      "hash": "ec3c0725a2e7e9554d174c43222eb602852e8909e78e1d65da1a8c3415ad6a2e"
    },
    {
      "id": "27947de0c766c5ac819bb0ab6af9041beb018ac3c8a6a1628d0ee111e98f2246",
      "text": "Go deeper:",
      "hash": "15ad3d88c6733d9b257c322d3afecc9bce2b18558171007db87598c118ca17f9"
    },
    {
      "id": "2c4cd5d3a24f24e2b5c8a21f70ab3cfe8bf0a918ce76cbbeab200a98e3c82440",
      "text": "join the waitlist for AI Coding for Real Engineers",
      "hash": "16c3492a8464a0859c944e287a9d433e9a2635f22a6bd8aad59f88c3e80ab732"
    },
    {
      "id": "95d71f42baa0d16b357c83d8dc21b85bf92437a9caec84d1b9fcc996dba9a26f",
      "text": "But let's imagine that we fix this. Instead of saving the transport in a single variable, we'd store it using an id where we could later retrieve it.",
      "hash": "c537b7f450adecfd7ef4718e6dca39eab672094b6f2b0f178ae5aa5e45820e1a"
    },
    {
      "id": "3550eb894f960bbf46731f06eb2bd277e5d9d8de9802f626b4acb2ee140a2f3a",
      "text": "Even if we did this, we'd still have a problem.",
      "hash": "aa7828a4e7eb153cc3f3bca05a1236fea526b4a806722e16b7047a640f80c2a1"
    },
    {
      "id": "816cd951a24743af13c28fa1a5cbfd2795d685d78534c44f6779046ec3faa173",
      "text": "This approach requires a stateful server.",
      "hash": "6f17ffa66da71125f7b10ac3263f915c73580a29a4a61b3e83446e274fdd32ae"
    },
    {
      "id": "112a9d8256bbcb65c3444d5b82be99a4f0c05f5225fb534ec3f37d1c328e9d57",
      "text": "We'd need to keep track of the transports in memory. If the server process exits, the transports would be lost.",
      "hash": "19dffe8e071f736ad208e2dcfa2ebb189c6dcb27dcfe38b8bd3ab0f2b28e0523"
    },
    {
      "id": "9d701cdcfa494007c131769b21455b7ec968c49e5b1b4cafcab7c0c76f09a91a",
      "text": "This puts constraints on how the server can be deployed.",
      "hash": "86927d60deb2eb93b3240cd97def1fe3f22eaa861c51889556d2e4de4de38b1a"
    },
    {
      "id": "83e11715d52484725a988af7126169d365827f4b851926de600b39931ffb9ca5",
      "text": "Serverless environments like Vercel or AWS Lambda would not work",
      "hash": "0f9e0f3db122c94691800edb760ec82da2d4d84bec9a37ebb12635da648c45e6"
    },
    {
      "id": "59a76792fdd1ea4ae3c82906ea9b7d1fb681aae240b7e383393af29b17eae0b9",
      "text": "- they dispose of in-memory state between requests.",
      "hash": "d97bc83418a050a534964214c49f48c6d27ab7c6da6adab8a08773a97bc760dc"
    },
    {
      "id": "04569fc7523cc096da5b3b46be1781c3ecb0826d70d6b9a587b87c2777c2fb43",
      "text": "We'd need to deploy it to a",
      "hash": "272622005ebe7097bb436ccb1e49dc1de0a2ae3ed70bfd9d172af99d54c991f9"
    },
    {
      "id": "e0e5d85122c284e85aa5303f56312d367ff7ce8fec4408a35f62e059598e6278",
      "text": "long-running server",
      "hash": "98dfa915de5ab1df6d2795111d5cb573dff7736cef56e687534bf0929d50b21d"
    },
    {
      "id": "e11e129a1cfb8ad63aca2a189e94e4256b807b4820210de07e02d1ad79051e3b",
      "text": ", like a VPS.",
      "hash": "bde51f11d161085108ea75572863f039ae6f54cec826a8a7f1d026272ab31074"
    },
    {
      "id": "4b4127ff8cdd30eba15de17ec3dc8c943ff00bac7d5e43218ea079b28d980024",
      "text": "A better approach is to",
      "hash": "410b11327a2b319ac35537dba5439a4abcab7575afab788821a69235ebed6a54"
    },
    {
      "id": "a07247d6fccfa593250cb5731ef0ca9c7b795bfb9321ecb08590b1554b2e1b31",
      "text": "store the state in a database",
      "hash": "f45236e41545982c6e048b7c0b534224bb415d3b002362e604520b605b7ce62e"
    },
    {
      "id": "d746501eccdb20ecaf22cc895b65a279e28c9ae89149bfda01748210b868b09c",
      "text": ". We could use a key-value store like Redis.",
      "hash": "f0b7bf489d8ca8b1db836f6080abbfa3dd8253df09ed12380f8e8a2ff9c50deb"
    },
    {
      "id": "ece1f5ee9d836781c5dcc49ea71768d567a029589cbbafecfbfd591b1fccfb1f",
      "text": "Now the transport information is stored in Redis,",
      "hash": "485623aa952eeafd7145f30b0c80423c2d89f6d801d2bc4056e0390406cd9cda"
    },
    {
      "id": "1a92f80720c292cb4b52973e0cfd8050911393b4b21ee2383c6e04a8e0519261",
      "text": "the server can be stateless",
      "hash": "69fbd4301dfbe26efa44e0b070447114cb40c82639e34948824f49bb0898aeb6"
    },
    {
      "id": "ec0b0644cac5e22ad47083f06fbd6e93181141f943feae1a82ed901bb70ad5c6",
      "text": ". This means it can be deployed to serverless environments.",
      "hash": "09843d020a1225e20988114e487530006502c99a45f897c60257402aa1267026"
    },
    {
      "id": "9f1d51ca028c6b7b4b7201aec56d7536d91c9e974f701d96ea656a1aefa0d70d",
      "text": "This is the approach that",
      "hash": "f2764e3ad1e1fdeb75f63dfff8e1274a7a7556a2880d0cbd36d002811c607b81"
    },
    {
      "id": "86cfaea59cf9cbc5bb0277e56e10df8ea17373f386df64c41a3be908fe0279e4",
      "text": "has taken. I recommend",
      "hash": "02f830db37b447fe55143ff698b9b5487a354c3149a312bc73c3397ca6db3acc"
    },
    {
      "id": "e96b9bfffeb2c5647053bd134a50a98b7e2d952634468de6d310ffd080a21eea",
      "text": "checking out",
      "hash": "7a3686d617901171c51c4b0a6fef9798d7fc773e0293d1b2f613c31134c88d3f"
    },
    {
      "id": "304c961d6e3227e66e376d76ed3bc5fb622b8a527ca91b10ce3145f56a445bc4",
      "text": "their repo",
      "hash": "1556ef8c52f80d30687dadfa66cda10ca739cd0b3f5190270d08978588a26968"
    },
    {
      "id": "b37111832a6cacde19fe390180eaa73ed09de0217c0a566bbbcb0384c1322c57",
      "text": "to learn more.",
      "hash": "f4ee0f23a4f18c0105f109fc6531ef5636464a01183c6fe5168a728c4cacb30e"
    },
    {
      "id": "720c5dbf661f12857d600a45bcc1d912bdf263cd9c66c1a5aa1aec2e6c88b546",
      "text": "While their repo is designed to work with Vercel, it",
      "hash": "aab9c086757e50eafc5a7ebad24cf60b98a66b437cacc9908249642022815a17"
    },
    {
      "id": "7c8467a436bf84ff83fe529361f4ec0f9493af276bdf2dc62ab1cf6f798c7c74",
      "text": "can be adapted to fit to any serverless platform",
      "hash": "7887bab2d6c03677fb3da20333339d2f20ef2febc0069f80819069df183607f2"
    },
    {
      "id": "dc8987eea36f23be5ef9e057d834f28b76818885398e3a19e70e5f42e4e6fdea",
      "text": "MCP servers are",
      "hash": "8eb8a0a7448f721eaaeb7fc97ca0a5b71edbb55f8b3e4e41bb9d1c6377801f61"
    },
    {
      "id": "bb1861e424e64116032a2fe49d2dce53accbeaa37a526ab5420dffaf2691caf3",
      "text": "by nature. But by storing the state in a database, we can deploy them to serverless environments.",
      "hash": "fb3a4fe08f11e42081eda62f92377e70d67477253e9fb02ed686c037f5f96f91"
    },
    {
      "id": "b5030bee44a0c906d1d880d060ba798554a1bc5071bc900dd9fb6f06cb524044",
      "text": "This would be my recommended approach for deploying MCP servers to production.",
      "hash": "9d2bf1d35e020d4da6f079eadc87074a1d5b5f480f763d84c4ba9a67177f73a6"
    },
    {
      "id": "0c9def3557437d436e8e5509f49c8ca877a2c9c71b1802916d534de1b52fffaa",
      "text": "However, it does beg the question: was there a way of designing this protocol so that the service could be",
      "hash": "cdbb2b0016559e64bb80387deedfd72a34afaf7ae0bef3c5a53b33ae57eb5f4b"
    },
    {
      "id": "f700f7b17503a3578fbc523954fdea26a3c2075719f1e308e2be90da2c38470a",
      "text": "Having to hook up a key-value store feels like more overhead than necessary. Could the client not store the state instead?",
      "hash": "482338d0345fa5c19077ae6f4618f1babce3ff356ee9998620b3ecdd8a1bcfb8"
    },
    {
      "id": "633a040783558135911f5cda3959272ec6c2751093393c290d9799129c5628d2",
      "text": "I'll explore this in a future article.",
      "hash": "9d6850e1aed1dd87584cebca6e9f0674c29d521fe500de34a856b32d00866395"
    },
    {
      "id": "36a214113158e6ce43c478d345c7cbf1461531793ced8798cd161fe61981260a",
      "text": "Share on X",
      "hash": "78d21bbf6b047944ec42890d28e151c61dbab35213fc65cc7be70c0c19c24407"
    },
    {
      "id": "ccba2e56504ec7df4fe98298620f27a09484cbe87e64100a8958ccfa93aedd81",
